  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nShortwave trough over the Canadian Prairies and NE Montana will\nbring rain showers early this morning to mainly the western half\nof the forecast area. The trough will move to the east this\nmorning which will allow the showers to diminish around 12z or\nsunrise. Clouds in the northeast are low enough in some areas \nthat could end up reaching the ground and create some fog. At the\nsame time, there are areas of clear skies with moist ground that \ncould allow for some fog this morning. Will mention patchy fog to \ncover the fog possibilities. \n\nAn upper ridge builds into Montana today along with surface high\npressure. Skies will gradually clear today and highs will be\nsomewhat warmer than yesterday but still below normal for mid\nAugust. \n\nA disturbance late tonight and Sunday morning will bring chances \nfor showers to areas south of Fort Peck Lake.\n\nSunday will be warmer with highs in the upper 70s to mid 80s with\nlight winds. An upper level disturbance Sunday night will bring \nchances for showers and thunderstorms to the area. \n\nAnother disturbance along with a cold front will bring chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms Monday night and Tuesday. \n\nUpper ridge builds into the area for Wednesday, Thursday and\nFriday with a return to warmer and drier conditions for the end \nof the week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo deviations from NBM this morning.  \n\nLow confidence of chances for showers south of Fort Peck Lake late\ntonight and Sunday morning.\n\nHigh confidence on drier weather today, tonight and Sunday\nmorning. Moderate confidence on shower and thunderstorm chances\nSunday night, Monday night and Tuesday.",
